equests.jsonl, rounds.jsonl, candidate_sets.parquet, topk_sidecar.npz, timing_microbench.json, oracle_report.md, metrics.json, failure_cases.jsonl, and .enoch/project_decision.json. Capture top-k, entropy, margins, accept lengths, latency, candidate-vocab coverage, n-gram/suffix hits, and grammar frontier stats without storing full logits or private text. Run 384 generations (~155k max new tokens) across agentic_loop, json_tool, code_edit, math_reasoning, open_chat, and long_context prompts at temperatures 0.0 and 0.7, with AR/EAGLE-3 mini-slices optional and non-blocking.","kill_condition":"Stop the whole line if no branch clears continue thresholds, best modeled end-to-end gain is below 5%, public prompt subset does not reproduce the private signal, measurement noise remains above 5% after three repeated timing passes, or instrumentation cannot produce the first oracle report within two engineering days.","likely_failure_modes":["DFlash instrumentation overhead distorts the measured bottleneck","No branch clears modeled gain thresholds","Private-prompt signal fails to reproduce on public prompts","DFlash model setup consumes the engineering budget","Trace volume grows too large without full-logit safeguards"],"machine_target":"gb10","mechanism":"Run Qwen3-8B with z-lab/Qwen3-8B-DFlash-b16, log per-round speculative decoding features and lightweight sidecars, then compute offline oracle analyses for all five candidate branches from the same trace.","model":"gpt-5.5","novelty_comparison":"This candidate supersedes the individually admitted speculative-decoding branch ideas by producing one shared DFlash trace and deterministic oracle report before branch implementation. It is not another branch; it is the branch-selection harness.","novelty_score":9.0,"parent_project_id":"","parent_run_id":"","priority":"High","prompt_version":"manual_unified_spec_trace_oracle_2026-05-19","provider":"chatgpt_pro_manual_import","provider_model":"ChatGPT Pro","raw_candidate_json":{"content_sha256":"6dd10d5509c86c0a01338aa3d5c07ccbc27916183b32fdb9e389781081deafa6","operator_instruction":"ingest as one unified trace/oracle project, not five separate branches","reference_urls":[{"idx":"1","title":"[2603.03251] Speculative Speculative Decoding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.03251?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"idx":"2","title":"GitHub - z-lab/dflash: DFlash: Block Diffusion for Flash Speculative Decoding \u00b7 GitHub","url":"https://github.com/z-lab/dflash"},{"idx":"3","title":"EAGLE-3: Scaling up Inference Acceleration of Large Language Models via Training-Time Test","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.01840?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"idx":"4","title":"Generating Structured Outputs from Language Models: Benchmark and Studies","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.10868?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"idx":"5","title":"Speculative Decoding with a Speculative Vocabulary","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.13836?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"idx":"6","title":"Extreme Speculative Decoding for Emerging AI Applications","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.04975?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"idx":"7","title":"Guiding LLMs The Right Way: Fast, Non-Invasive ...","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2403.06988v1?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}],"source_file":"new-chatgpt-pro-ideas-05-19-more.md"},"required_evidence":["DFlash baseline metrics","per-round trace schema validation","oracle metrics table for all five branches","decision matrix output","failure cases","public/private partition comparison","project decision artifact"],"risk_notes":"Main risk is infrastructure cost before signal. The plan explicitly caps instrumentation to two engineering days, avoids full logits, uses simulated controllers before online policies, uses n-gram maps before suffix trees, and shadows grammar without constraining generation.","sandbox":"danger-full-access","score_breakdown":{"accessibility_weighted":22.5,"admit_threshold":72.0,"falsifiability_weighted":22.0,"feasibility_weighted":11.9,"hard_failure_pena